+- **Other deferred differences:** spawn's final decomposition-only stop wins over earlier execution prose. Swarm's missing-proxy STOP/fallback disagreement is disclosed without promising a real run or fallback. Load's example-only checkpoint option is not executor recovery. Task's classification-before-tools prose does not waive the governing skill-first rule; do not duplicate its internals here. Active plugin copies can lack skills or safeguards even when command files exist: verify them or report unavailable/contract gap. Planning depth is not a guarantee of multi-session plan generation, while implement execution is resumable. Validate-tests needs a real YAML suite. Startup status messages do not prove agent/PM activation.
+- **Retired framework identities:** estimate, the sc dispatcher, select-tool and task-mcp are not current runnable framework targets, even if readable installed remnants survive. Explicit deprecated metadata and verified canonical retirement outrank readability. Answer retirement questions with the underlying intent and a current independently verified alternative; do not trust task-mcp's stale replacement metadata or resurrect bypass flags. Do not delete, update or reinstall anything automatically. Independently authored installed-only/custom commands remain eligible; uncertain ownership of a same-name override needs clarification, not blanket rejection.
+- **Evidence:** static routing assertions, generated recommendation results and actual specialized-command execution are distinct. Do not report fabricated quality scores, timing, savings or test counts. A report-only stop can still write tool-owned artifacts; memory, product edits, Git operations and external publication must be described separately.
 
